        "content": "Prov 02. Följ användarens instruktioner. Ange osäkerhet när underlag saknas."
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Skriv endast Python-kod för parse_size(s). Tillåt valfritt antal blanksteg runt hela strängen, sedan ett eller flera ASCII-siffror och exakt en av enheterna B, KiB, MiB (skiftlägeskänsligt), utan mellanrum emellan. Returnera heltalsbyte, med multiplikatorerna 1, 1024, 1048576. All annan indata som är sträng ska ge ValueError, inklusive decimaler, minustecken, Unicode-siffror, extra radslut inne i strängen och saknad enhet. ' 001KiB\n' är giltigt. Använd standardbiblioteket."
      }
    ]
  },
  "started_unix": 1791356513.2309065,
  "wall_s": 89.84275219799747,
  "first_token_s": 16.584357238003577,
  "content": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_size(s: str) -> int:\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a string\")\n    \n    # Pattern: optional leading whitespace, one or more ASCII digits, exactly one unit (B, KiB, MiB), optional trailing whitespace\n    # The unit must be case-sensitive.\n    # We use ^ and $ to ensure the entire string matches the pattern after stripping? \n    # No, the problem says \"valfritt antal blanksteg runt hela strängen\", which implies leading/trailing whitespace is allowed.\n    # But \"utan mellanrum emellan\" means no space between number and unit.\n    # \"All annan indata ... ska ge ValueError\"\n    \n    # Let's construct a regex that matches:\n    # ^\\s*          : optional leading whitespace\n    # (\\d+)         : one or more ASCII digits (capturing group 1)\n    # (B|KiB|MiB)   : exactly one of the units (capturing group 2)\n    # \\s*$          : optional trailing whitespace\n    \n    # Note: \\d in Python regex matches Unicode digits by default unless re.ASCII is used.\n    # The problem states \"ASCII-siffror\" and \"Unicode-siffror\" should raise ValueError.\n    # So we must use re.ASCII flag or explicitly [0-9].\n    \n    pattern = r'^\\s*([0-9]+)(B|KiB|MiB)\\s*$'\n    match = re.match(pattern, s)\n    \n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid size format\")\n    \n    number_str = match.group(1)\n    unit = match.group(2)\n    \n    # Convert number to int\n    # Leading zeros are allowed (e.g., '001KiB')\n    value = int(number_str)\n    \n    multipliers = {\n        'B': 1,\n        'KiB': 1024,\n        'MiB': 1048576\n    }\n    \n    return value * multipliers[unit]\n```",
